From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:42:11 +0200
Subject: --no-launchers: no icon from a GOG installer either

A package made from a GOG.com setup_*.exe got the installer's
goggame-*.ico, converted to /usr/share/pixmaps/gdp-PACKAGE.png when
python3-pil is installed, as an optional file of every package that
isn't music or documentation. That icon is for a menu entry, which
--no-launchers leaves to another package, and it is made on the fly, so
nothing can know its checksum beforehand: Walnut's import refused
quake-rerelease from GOG's Quake Enhanced installer over it. With
--no-launchers the icon is neither extracted nor added; the man page
says so.

Forwarded: not yet (goes with --no-launchers)

diff --git a/doc/game-data-packager.6 b/doc/game-data-packager.6
--- a/doc/game-data-packager.6
+++ b/doc/game-data-packager.6
@@ -129,8 +129,10 @@ If files are downloaded, save them to \fIDIRECTORY\fR.
 .TP
 .B \-\-no\-launchers
 Do not put menu entries (.desktop files) or their icons into the packages.
-Only the Doom family (Doom, Heretic, Hexen and related games) writes them;
-use this when another package provides the launchers.
+The Doom family (Doom, Heretic, Hexen and related games) writes them, and any
+game made from a GOG.com setup_*.exe gets the installer's icon as
+/usr/share/pixmaps/gdp-PACKAGE.png; use this when another package provides
+the launchers.
 .TP
 \fB\-\-progress\-fd\fR \fIFD\fR
 Write machine-readable progress to file descriptor \fIFD\fR, one line per
diff --git a/game_data_packager/build.py b/game_data_packager/build.py
--- a/game_data_packager/build.py
+++ b/game_data_packager/build.py
@@ -1444,7 +1444,9 @@ class PackagingTask:
                     extra_icon = None
                     basename = os.path.basename(found_name)
                     extension = os.path.splitext(basename)[1]
-                    if basename.startswith('setup_') and extension == '.exe':
+                    # --no-launchers: no menu icon from GOG's .ico either
+                    if (self.launchers and basename.startswith('setup_')
+                            and extension == '.exe'):
                         with InnoSetup(
                             os.path.abspath(found_name),
                             verbose=self.verbose,
@@ -2296,7 +2298,8 @@ class PackagingTask:
                 hf = HashedFile.from_file(icon_name, opened)
                 opened.close()
         for package in packages:
-            if package.data_type not in ('music', 'documentation'):
+            if (self.launchers
+                    and package.data_type not in ('music', 'documentation')):
                 icon_name = self.get_extra_icon_name(package)
                 wf = self.game.files[icon_name]
                 assert package.optional_files is not None
